  "uncertain": [
    "qwiic: the image lists the four Qwiic signals in a callout without showing which physical connector pin each belongs to; position order is inferred from the label list order.",
    "gravity-analog: this 3-row block sits mid-board, so which row is the \"outer\" row for 2xN/3xN ordering is a judgment call (GND row taken as nearest the left board edge).",
    "USB-C callout (GND, VBUS, USB D-, USB D+ with GPIO19, GND with GPIO20) labels USB signals but shows no individual connector positions; not transcribed as a connector. GPIO20 appears aligned beside GND rather than a USB data line."
  ],
  "notes": "Board shown carries an ESP32-S3-MINI-1 and Renesas P-port names, plus extra 3-row S/5V/GND headers not on a plain UNO layout. Labels written with \"GPI0\" in the image (GPI042, GPI041, GPI043, GPI00, GPI044) recorded with letter O per the O/0 context rule. RX/TX/L LED pads, RESET button, LEDs (LED_BUTLTIN, TX_LED, RX_LED, Power) and DC jack skipped. IN/OUT tags kept as short notes."
